    "description": "A storefront product filter rendered as a row of colour swatches, one per value, multi-select. Each swatch paints the colour the value stands for, so a shopper picks by sight rather than by reading a word.",
    "useWhen": [
      "the facet IS a colour — a Color attribute axis, or a tag set that maps onto real colours",
      "the values are more recognisable as swatches than as words",
      "the palette is small enough to sit in a row or two without scrolling"
    ],
    "avoidWhen": [
      "the values are not colours — a size or a brand in a swatch is a coloured square nobody can read",
      "the palette is large and unfamiliar, where a labelled checkbox list is faster to scan",
      "only one value may be chosen at a time — use the Radio filter"
    ],
    "contentTips": [
      "give every value a colour: an unmapped value still renders, as an empty ringed swatch, and a shopper cannot tell what it stands for",
      "keep the swatch large enough to be a comfortable tap target on a phone — the size is per-breakpoint, so it can grow there",
      "point it at the attribute axis that actually holds colours, not at the whole attribute source"
    ],
