    "description": "A storefront product filter rendered as a wrapped row of tappable pills, one per value, multi-select. The chip carries its own label, so a shopper picks by reading rather than by aiming at a small box.",
    "useWhen": [
      "the values are short words a shopper scans rather than reads — sizes, tags, materials",
      "several values should fit on one line instead of stacking down the page",
      "the filter sits in a horizontal bar above the products rather than in a sidebar"
    ],
    "avoidWhen": [
      "the labels are long: a chip that wraps its own text reads as a broken button",
      "only one value may be chosen at a time — use the Radio filter",
      "the values are colours — a Color swatch says more than the word for it"
    ],
    "contentTips": [
      "keep labels to a word or two so the row wraps predictably at every breakpoint",
      "the columns control is what fits chips per line; lower it on mobile rather than shrinking the text",
      "a chip with no products is hidden on the storefront, so a sparse-looking row usually means the catalog, not the filter"
    ],
