    "description": "A storefront PRICE filter rendered as a track with two draggable handles and the two bound labels under it. It writes a single continuous range, so a shopper can ask for anything between the ends rather than picking one of a few bands.",
    "useWhen": [
      "the catalog spans a wide price range and no small set of bands describes it well",
      "the page has room for a horizontal control — a slider needs width to be usable",
      "shoppers filter by budget rather than by a named tier"
    ],
    "avoidWhen": [
      "the store sells at three or four price points — a Checkbox filter with named bands is faster and states the bands out loud",
      "the filter must sit in a narrow column: a short track makes every drag imprecise",
      "the filter is for anything other than price — the other four filters take values, this one takes a range"
    ],
    "contentTips": [
      "set the bounds to the real cheapest and dearest products; a max far above the catalog leaves most of the track dead",
      "the two labels are your own words — write them in the currency a shopper reads, since the element never formats money itself",
      "a shopper can also arrive with a range in the URL, so the handles show what the page is already filtered to"
    ],
