    "description": "A single text field inside a form: a label, the box the visitor types into, and an optional line of help underneath. Switches between a one-line input and a multi-line box, and can be pointed at a customer column so what is typed reaches the customer record rather than only the response log.",
    "useWhen": [
      "The answer is free text a visitor writes themselves — a name, an email address, a message.",
      "The answer belongs on the customer record: point the field at the matching column instead of collecting it twice.",
      "A longer answer is expected — turn on multi-line so the box looks like the amount of writing being asked for."
    ],
    "avoidWhen": [
      "The answer is one of a known set — a choice control is faster to answer and impossible to misspell.",
      "The answer is a quantity or a date; those have their own fields, which validate and format for the visitor.",
      "The same column is already collected by another field in this form — one column takes one value, and the form will be refused."
    ],
    "contentTips": [
      "Label the field with what you want, not with the format you want it in. Put the format in the help line.",
      "A placeholder is not a label: it disappears the moment someone types, so anything they need while writing belongs in the label or the help line.",
      "Mark a field required only if you would genuinely discard the response without it."
    ],
