    "description": "A field that lets a visitor attach a file to their response — a photo, a video or a PDF. Accepts one kind at a time, optionally several files at once, and the attachments arrive with the response rather than separately, so a refused form never leaves a stray upload behind.",
    "useWhen": [
      "The answer is a document or an image the visitor already has — a CV, a receipt, a photo of a damaged item.",
      "Seeing the thing is faster than reading a description of it: a support form for a broken product, a print order.",
      "Several pieces of one answer belong together — turn on multiple uploads and set the limit to how many you will actually look at."
    ],
    "avoidWhen": [
      "The answer can be typed. A file is slower to send on a phone and slower to read afterwards.",
      "You want more than one KIND of file in a single field — a field accepts images, videos or PDFs, not a mixture. Use one field per kind, each labelled for what it wants.",
      "The form is meant to be answered in seconds; asking for an attachment is the step people abandon."
    ],
    "contentTips": [
      "Say in the label or the help line which formats you accept and roughly how large a file may be — a visitor who finds out by being refused usually leaves.",
      "The button label is what a visitor reads before choosing; \"Choose a photo\" tells them more than \"Upload\".",
      "Only mark it required if a response without the attachment is genuinely of no use to you.",
      "Keep the file limit to what you will really open — every extra file is storage the site is billed for."
    ],
