    "description": "A date asked as separate boxes — day, month and year, optionally with a time box, or the time alone (the Format setting: Date & time / Only date / Only time). Nothing opens; the visitor types what they already know.",
    "useWhen": [
      "The date is one the visitor knows by heart — a birthday, an anniversary. Typing it is faster than steering a calendar back through hundreds of months.",
      "The date is far from today. A picker starts at the current month, which is the wrong end of the journey for a year of birth."
    ],
    "avoidWhen": [
      "The visitor is choosing a date rather than recalling one — a delivery day, an appointment. A calendar shows which days exist and which weekday each one falls on.",
      "A single free-typed value would do. If the answer is one number — an age, a year — a number field reads better than a lone date box."
    ],
    "contentTips": [
      "Pick the Format by what the answer needs: Only date for a birthday, Date & time for an appointment moment, Only time for opening hours or a preferred call time.",
      "Drop the year when the year adds nothing — a birthday greeting needs the day and the month, and asking for a birth year asks for the visitor’s age."
    ],
