    "description": "A store-driven dataset repeater: it renders ONE dataset-block template once per record — every product of a collection, or every collection of the store — laid out as a responsive grid or a row-by-row slide carousel. Each repeated card is bound to its own record, so a single authored template drives an entire listing.",
    "useWhen": [
      "Product listing sections — \"shop the collection\", featured products, related products — where every card reuses one layout",
      "Collection listings: a grid or carousel of the store's collections, each card showing that collection's image and name",
      "You want to design ONE card (image + title + price + actions) and have it repeat across many records automatically"
    ],
    "avoidWhen": [
      "Displaying a SINGLE product or collection (a product-detail buy box) — use a plain dataset-block, with no repeater",
      "Static marketing cards that do not read live store data — use content-list or flex-section",
      "A single dataset field such as only the title, price or image — use that specific dataset node instead"
    ],
    "contentTips": [
      "Always add exactly one dataset-block child as the repeated item template; every row clones that exact structure and styling",
      "The dataset-block template — and every dataset node inside it — must carry the SAME config.datasetSource as this repeater. Each node reads its OWN key, so a collection list whose card omits it leaves that card on the product default: it binds product.url, no product context reaches a collection row, and the card publishes with no link, so clicking it does nothing",
      "config.datasetSource picks the ENTITY: \"product\" for a product list, \"category\" for a collection list. It is what derives the node's binding target (product::product_list / category::collection_list)",
      "Product lists: config.collectionType \"all_products\" renders the whole catalog, \"collection\" renders the one named by config.collectionId, \"related\" renders the PAGE PRODUCT's neighbours — the products sharing one of its collections, minus itself",
      "Use \"related\" for a cross-sell shelf on a product page (\"Sản phẩm liên quan\" / \"You may also like\"). It reads no collectionId — its axis is whatever collections the page product is filed under — and it renders nothing on a page that names no product, so pair it with an emptyStateId if the section must never be blank",
      "Collection lists: config.collectionListType \"all_collections\" renders every collection; \"custom_collections\" renders specials.collectionIds, in that order",
      "config.quantity caps how many records render; config.itemsPerRow is the row size (grid columns / slide page size) and style.gap is the space between cards — both are per-breakpoint",
      "config.layout \"grid\" for a multi-row grid, \"slide\" for row-by-row carousel behaviour",
      "Navigation and pagination only matter when layout is \"slide\". The arrows exist while config.listNavIcon names an icon (clearing it turns them off); the dots exist while paginationItemWidth and paginationItemHeight are both above 0",
      "config.loadingMode is how a GRID list offers the REST of its feed once config.quantity rows are on screen: \"none\" (the default — those rows and nothing more), \"pagination\" (a numbered pager, each page its own URL), \"load_more\" (a button that appends the next page in place) or \"scroll_more\" (the same append, triggered by reaching the end). Set it whenever the listing is a real catalogue rather than a fixed shelf of featured rows",
      "With any loadingMode but \"none\", config.quantity stops meaning \"the cap\" and becomes the PAGE SIZE — the same number doing a different job, so a paginated grid wants a full page of rows (8-12) rather than the 4 a featured shelf shows",
      "loadingMode is ignored when layout is \"slide\": a carousel already pages through its feed with its arrows and dots, so setting both is two mechanisms over one feed",
      "specials.loadMoreLabel is the words on the \"load more\" button and is read by a SHOPPER, so write it in the store's language (\"Xem thêm\", \"Load more\"). It only renders when loadingMode is \"load_more\"",
      "The pager and the button carry their own look, all per-breakpoint: pagerAlign / pagerSpacing / pagerItemGap / pagerItemWidth / pagerItemHeight / pagerItemBg / pagerItemColor / pagerItemBorder* plus the pagerItemActive* and pagerItemHover* families; moreAlign / moreSpacing / moreHeight / morePaddingX / moreBg / moreColor / moreBorder* plus moreHover*. Leave them unset to inherit the plain default look",
      "Fill the template with dataset fields (media-dataset, text-dataset title, pricing-dataset, add-to-cart button) so each card shows real store data",
      "Style the list-dataset for outer spacing, width and carousel controls; style the child dataset-block for the card itself"
    ],
    "semantics": [
      "dataset",
      "store",
      "ecommerce",
      "product",
      "collection",
      "repeater",
      "list",
      "grid",
      "carousel",
      "pagination",
      "load more"
    ]
