    "description": "The EMPTY STATE of a store surface: the container rendered in place of the real content when there is none — a list whose feed has no records, a cart with no lines, a product card with no product. An icon, a headline, a line of guidance, and optionally a button back to something that does have content.",
    "useWhen": [
      "a listing has to say something when the store has no products, articles or collections yet",
      "a collection page can legitimately resolve to nothing and should not render blank",
      "a cart, or a single product card, has to say what is missing instead of showing ghost content"
    ],
    "avoidWhen": [
      "as a standalone block: this element only renders through the surface that owns it, which creates it",
      "to hold the card design — that is the list template, repeated once per record"
    ],
    "contentTips": [
      "keep it short: what is missing, and what the visitor can do instead",
      "a link back to the catalogue or the blog index turns a dead end into a route onward",
      "it is what a real visitor sees, so write it for a shopper, not for the site owner"
    ],
    "semantics": [
      "empty-state",
      "list",
      "repeater",
      "placeholder",
      "container"
    ]
